  "worked_solution": "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{4}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n(-3)+8\\,=\\,{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\u21d2\\,{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{7}(2-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{7}1\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,3{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot x{|}_{1}^{7}\\,-\\,3(5) \\\\  & =2(7-1)-15 \\\\  & =12-15 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
